bdr:NT84450521E8C91702
   a             bdo:Note ;
   bdo:noteText  "the issue of multiple nagarjunas has often been discussed in indological literature; the policy of the tbrc is to use the form nagarjuna for all of the works attributed to nagarjuna,  works on madhyamika philosophy, writings on medicine, and tantric and devotional works; at least some of these are the works of tibetan authors regarded as embodiments of nagarjuna such as 'bri gung 'jig rten mgon po"@en .

